# A catalog stores the same count with different numeric lexical forms.
# With --owl2rl, their exact values agree and an out-of-range byte produces a conflict.
# This shows partial OWL 2 RL datatype reasoning and positive AllDifferent consequences.
# Rule semantics: W3C OWL 2 Profiles, section 4.3.

@prefix : <https://example.org/catalog#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

# Equal numeric values can substitute even when their RDF terms differ.
:left :count "01"^^xsd:integer .
:right :count "1.0"^^xsd:decimal .

# A range assertion cannot make 129 a member of the byte value space.
:byteCount rdfs:range xsd:byte .
:broken :byteCount 129 .

# Explicitly distinct catalog items also acquire pairwise differentFrom triples.
:items a owl:AllDifferent ; owl:distinctMembers (:left :right) .
